# The mirror of the login on sites through the Russian node amf (task 113,
# docs/ops/ru-node.md), for the countries where the name of
# PLUMA_OAUTH_DOMAIN is blocked: the pages of the provider in links, as
# that site serves them. links tells the provider by the Host header, so
# the snippet hands it PLUMA_OAUTH_DOMAIN: the provider is the same one,
# with the same issuer in its tokens. Its cookies are the browser's for the
# mirror's own name. The name points at the node, whose nginx passes the
# client's TLS as it came, behind PROXY v1, through the plumaru tunnel to
# port 8443 here, as for the edge (ru-edge.caddy): TLS ends here with
# home's certificate, and X-Forwarded-For names the address of the PROXY
# header, the visitor's.
#
# The Caddyfile imports this file only when PLUMA_RU_OAUTH_DOMAIN is set
# (docker-compose.web.yaml), for the reason of ru-site.caddy. A request of
# the node without the PROXY header is aborted first, as there.
{$PLUMA_RU_OAUTH_DOMAIN}:8443 {
	@unwrapped remote_ip {$PLUMA_RU_EDGE_PROXY_FROM}
	route {
		abort @unwrapped
		handle {
			import pluma_oauth
		}
	}
}
